<description>
Recolor every object whose shape matches a teal template object to teal.

Input structure
- A black-background lattice contains many monochrome connected objects in blue or red.
- One or more teal objects are already drawn in places where such objects have been recolored.
- Shape identity is translation-normalized and uses 8-connectivity, so diagonal contact can join one template.

Rule
- Treat each teal connected object as a shape template.
- Among non-black, non-teal objects, find the unique source color whose object masks match those teal templates.
- Recolor every object of that source color with a matching normalized mask to teal; preserve all other pixels.

Key insight
- The teal pixels are examples of completed objects, not a path or paint source; their masks select all same-shaped objects elsewhere in the lattice.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "non-black, non-teal 8-connected object s",
  "dst": "teal 8-connected template object d",
  "match_cond": "s.normalized_mask == d.normalized_mask",
  "transform": "recolor every matched s to teal; preserve the teal templates and all unmatched pixels",
  "symbol_instructions": "teal objects provide both the template masks and the output color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 17-27 rows x cols, always square (H==W) [observed]
  colors: black(0) background, blue(1) and red(2) as lattice/source (either can be lattice), teal(8) for templates
  lattice:
    definition: one color forms a single 8-connected component spanning the grid
    structure: full lattice-color rows and columns divide the grid into cells; cells are 2-3 pixels wide [observed]
    pixel_fraction: 42-66%
  source_objects:
    definition: 8-connected components of the other non-bg color (not lattice, not teal)
    count: 19-56 objects, sizes 1-8 pixels, bbox at most 3x3
    pixel_fraction: 18-35%
  background: 17-23% of pixels [observed]
  symmetry: normalized grid (teal -> source_color) is transpose-symmetric (grid == grid.T) [observed]
  wallpaper: the row-type sequence and column-type sequence are identical (consequence of transpose symmetry)
  teal_templates:
    count: 1-2 template objects, 1-2 distinct shapes
    pixel_count: 2-5 per template, bbox at most 3x3
  matching: source objects matching any template shape = 3-6 (additional to templates themselves)
  rule: >
    Find 8-connected teal objects as shape templates. Among source-color objects,
    find all with matching normalized mask. Recolor those to teal. Only one non-bg
    non-teal color has matching objects (the source color, not the lattice color).

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N in [17..27] (odd preferred for symmetry). Pick lattice_color and source_color from {1,2}.
    2. Build a 1D type sequence of length N using letters {L, m, s} where L=lattice-line, m=mixed(bg), s=source+lattice. Use this for both rows and cols to ensure transpose symmetry.
    3. Fill grid[r,c] based on (type[r], type[c]): if either is L -> lattice_color; if both m -> 0; if one m and one s -> source_color; if both s -> source_color or lattice_color (vary to create diverse shapes). Ensure grid == grid.T.
    4. Verify lattice_color forms exactly one 8-connected component. Find all 8-connected source objects.
    5. Pick 1-2 template shapes from the source objects (each must have >=2 additional source objects with the same normalized mask). Recolor one instance of each template shape to teal -> this is the INPUT.
    6. Recolor ALL matching source objects to teal -> this is the OUTPUT.
    7. Validate: only one non-bg non-teal color has matching objects; total matching >= 3.
